WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.810
Thick fog.

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:02.939
Some airliners land themselves.

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:05.617
A radio altimeter measures
its height above

00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:08.001
the ground, very precisely.

00:00:08.011 --> 00:00:09.944
Near the ground, it eases the power

00:00:09.954 --> 00:00:11.894
back and raises the nose:

00:00:11.904 --> 00:00:12.859
the flare.

00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:15.944
Often three independent
autopilots fly it, for

00:00:15.954 --> 00:00:16.851
backup.

00:00:16.861 --> 00:00:19.251
After touchdown, it can keep the plane

00:00:19.261 --> 00:00:20.697
on the centreline.

00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:22.607
So how does it find the runway?

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.572
Radio beams from the ground:

00:00:24.582 --> 00:00:26.497
one lines it up, one sets its

00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:27.732
slope down.
